4618,1974-014,1974-014-01,73-1055,1974,"BOWMAN TRANSPORTATION, INC. v. ARKANSAS-BEST FREIGHT SYSTEM, INC., et al.",8.0,1.0,"These are five consolidated cases involving 13 motor carriers who filed for certificates with the Interstate Commerce Commission (ICC) in order to conduct business between the southwestern and southeastern United States.  The ICC rejected all but three applications.  Bowman Transportation, Inc., one of the approved applicants, asked for more authority than initially set out in their application.  The ICC granted that authority, and the competing motor carriers sued in U.S. District Court for the Western District of Arkansas to annul the certificate.  The district court found the ICC’s actions arbitrary and capricious.  The court voided the certificates and permanently enjoined the ICC from issuing them.  The Supreme Court heard this case on direct appeal.
