8090,1993-082,1993-082-01,93-644,1993,"HONDA MOTOR CO., LTD., et al. v. KARL L. OBERG",8.0,1.0,"Karl Oberg was driving an all-terrain vehicle when it overturned, causing him severe, permanent injuries. The jury in his trial assessed almost $1 million in compensatory damages, and an additional $5 million in punitive damages. A 1910 amendment to the Oregon state constitution prohibited judicial review of jury awards.
